EVP First — Timeline Rendering Specification
1. Purpose
The timeline is the primary longitudinal visualization of a patient’s bladder preservation journey. This specification defines:

how events are fetched

how they are merged

how they are sorted

how they are grouped

how they are displayed

how they are expanded

how they are styled

It ensures the frontend and backend remain perfectly aligned.

2. Inputs to the Timeline
The timeline receives four datasets from the backend:

Master record

Diagnosis records

Treatment records

Events records (normalized clinical events)

All datasets must be merged into a single chronological event stream.

3. Required Event Shape
Every event rendered in the timeline must include:

uid

masterId

eventType

eventDate

eventSummary

eventDetails

payload

If any of these are missing, the event is excluded and logged.

4. Event Merging Rules
Step 1 — Convert master/diagnosis/treatment into events
The frontend transforms:

Master → “Patient created” event

Diagnosis → “Diagnosis” event

Treatment → “Treatment_Start” event

These follow the same shape as backend events.

Step 2 — Combine with Events table
All events from Airtable’s Events table are appended.

Step 3 — Deduplicate
Events with identical:

eventType

eventDate

uid

are merged, preferring the most complete eventDetails.

5. Sorting Rules
Events are sorted by:

Primary: eventDate (ascending)

Secondary: clinical priority

Diagnosis

TURBT

Imaging

Cystoscopy

Cytology

Molecular

Treatment

Recurrence/Progression

QoL

Administrative

Tertiary: creation order (UID timestamp)

If two events share the same date, they appear in the priority order above.

6. Grouping Rules
Events are grouped by calendar date.

Example:

Code
2024-01-01
  - CT Abd/Pelvis
  - Urine cytology
  - QoL assessment
If a date has >4 events, the group collapses with a “Show more” toggle.

7. Rendering Rules
7.1 TimelineEventCard
Each event is rendered using the TimelineEventCard component.

Card structure
Header: eventType + icon

Subheader: eventSummary

Date: formatted eventDate

Body: collapsed by default

Expand: shows eventDetails

Icons
Icons are mapped by category:

Diagnosis → 🧬

TURBT → 🔪

Imaging → 🖥️

Cystoscopy → 🔍

Cytology → 🧪

Molecular → 🧫

Treatment → 💊

Recurrence/Progression → ⚠️

QoL → 🙂

Administrative → 📄

Icons are consistent across the platform.

7.2 EventType → Color Mapping
Colors reinforce clinical meaning:

Category	Color
Diagnosis	Blue
TURBT	Indigo
Imaging	Teal
Cystoscopy	Green
Cytology	Lime
Molecular	Purple
Treatment	Orange
Recurrence/Progression	Red
QoL	Yellow
Administrative	Gray


Colors apply to:

card border

icon background

date marker

8. Expansion Rules
When expanded, the card shows:

eventDetails (structured)

payload (raw source)

“View full event” link (future feature)

Structured details
eventDetails is rendered as:

Code
Field: Value
Field: Value
Field: Value
Raw payload
Displayed in a collapsible JSON viewer.

9. Error Handling Rules
If an event cannot be rendered:

log to console (dev only)

show a placeholder card:

“Unrenderable event — see details”

include raw payload for debugging

If eventDate is invalid:

place event in “Unknown date” group at top

highlight card in red

10. Performance Rules
Batching
All events are rendered in a single React batch.

Memoization
useMemo is required for:

merged events

sorted events

grouped events

Virtualization (future)
If >300 events, switch to virtualized list.

11. Timeline Layout Rules
Mobile
vertical list

collapsed groups

minimal icons

Desktop
vertical list with date markers

expanded groups

full icons and colors

Spacing
16px between cards

24px between date groups

